[{:seon.task/name "a-commit-reaches-only-the-readers-of-what-it-moved"
  :seon.task/plan "DECISIONS 2026-11-15 (owner via root; reviewed by flow and deps; notes runtime-core-index-plan-2026-11-15.md and runtime-reactive-plan-2026-11-15.md). Owner: index and proofs first, fully proven, the least code for 90% of the value; the core lands WITH its first real callers, proved on them: the page walk's :readers (render/queue-what-moved!) moves onto the index in the same landing, measured on the standing root after web's stall fix (the walk's readers count and per-commit cost before and after, against the ~163M post-fix cold walk, never the 6.8B debug-tab draw); health's delta fold follows as the next landing on the same core. Two reader kinds: a delta fold (state + a commit's datoms -> state') for aggregates (health, laws, the reconciler index), and a reaction for point reads (a page's component). Feed: d/changes per owner (deps proved it complete: 0 of 40 differences were net changes [deps M result/d1d98078]; 5.8M against 26.2M ticks over 406 commits [result/aa42fbe8]); the writer's notice stays {:t :commit :program-t}, each owner reads its own change in its own step, :main is a sliding buffer (flow). MEASURED today's commit! [M root result/bcecbc16]: 53.6k / 538k / 4.41M ticks at 10 / 100 / 1,000 readers for a d=10 commit none read (~5.4k a reader); a hit reruns exactly its reader. Design (~25 lines in seon.ratom, nothing new in seon.db): the Store keeps {key #{reaction}} (seon.db/reads-add, reads-drop, readers) beside its watches and holds its owner; a reaction's run updates its keys in each Store it watches, dropping them on unwatch or dispose; a run whose *owner* is not the Store's sends {:seon.ratom/keys r ks} to the Store owner's port, never a direct set! (flow's hole: the same race is latent today in watches); commit! iterates the index value captured before its loop and wakes only (readers idx datoms); a watch that is not a reaction is still called; deleted: the per-reaction reads-touched? scan on a store change. Proofs, each red first: (a) a d=10 commit at 10, 100 and 1,000 readers within 2x (82x today); (b) a 10x larger store within 2x; (c) a hot [:a a] attribute read whole by 100 readers reruns exactly 100, the commit's own cost within its budget; (d) the rerun set equals today's reads-touched? scan, generatively, seeded with deps' cases (byte-array values, [:av] through a lookup ref or ident vs the eid, cardinality-one upserts and re-assertions, a schema datom (:all) and an attribute rename, fixnum key collisions), plus the stress run at root's REPL: main's last 100 real commits replayed into 1,000 real readers, one process, no load; (e) a cross-owner key update arrives as a message. An agent, not runtime, merges and tests it. The design below stays as the height-queue and owner-step background. THE PLAN item 11 (owner-approved order, 2026-11-15): the reactive core goes live, the render proc first. The index is seon.db/reads-add, reads-drop and readers (db.clj:1236-1260, written and tested, no src caller): each reaction's key set is added under it at its run's end and dropped at its next, replacing each reaction's own watch scan, so commit! is O(d): readers over the commit's datoms. The datoms come from the writer's commit notice (:ops), never a diff (agreed with deps). Render proc first: each view becomes a reaction over its store, fed by the render proc's :main notices. Deletes in that landing: the render proc's :read-index, reindex and touched (render/proc.clj:895-914), the walk's :readers and :db-keys (render.clj:351, 1258-1261), health's second diff (proc.clj:800). Proof kept: seon.render-test/a-move-of-main-is-diffed-once-for-every-walk. Estimate: per commit, d datoms x 5 keys x one map lookup (about 1k ticks at d = 12 [M, trial A1's prototype]) plus the readers' reruns; per reaction run, its keys' add and drop, O(keys). Health, the reconciler and test verdicts follow, each its own landing that deletes what it replaces (audit target/root/audits-2026-11-15/derived-values.md section 4). The plan below stays as the height-queue and owner-step design. Owner: runtime (owner 2026-11-14 21:20: runtime owns the reactive core). Analysis approved by root and flow (notes runtime-core-map/plan-advance-heights-owner-step.md). What exists [M]: seon.ratom/commit! notifies EVERY watch of the store and each reaction tests reads-touched? over the datoms: O(readers x d), 1.25M ticks for a commit no reader read at 1,489 readers (trial A1); seon.ratom/flush! runs its queue in arrival order and an auto-run reaction runs at once inside -handle-change, so a diamond's top runs once per path (3x, ctx-r1, A1). Design: advance! (store, new-db) diffs the held head and the new head once (datahike.db/datoms-diff of plain heads, never d/history or a view), looks each moved datom's 5 keys up in {key #{reader}} kept by each reader's run (keys gained added, lost dropped, never rebuilt whole; a schema datom touches every reader) and answers {reader [datoms]}; the flush is buckets by height (1 + max height of its reactive sources, kept on the reaction), always the lowest dirty reaction next, auto-run held to the flush; a source gained mid-flush with height >= the run's raises it and its ancestors (Jane Street Incremental's adjust-heights: state.ml add_parent, adjust_heights_heap.ml), moving queued nodes, and re-queues the run unnotified when that source is still queued; effects only from a settled run; a cycle is that run's typed :seon.ratom/cycle and the flush completes. Estimate: diff O(d log32 N) ~9k ticks and ~26 KB a datom at small d; lookup O(5d) ~1k ticks, constant in readers and N; index upkeep ~160 ticks a key gained or lost; flush O(r + h + sum a) (r re-runs, h depth, a ancestors raised); d = 10: ~0.6 ms. Deletes: commit!'s match over every watch, flush!'s arrival order, auto-run's run inside -handle-change. Proofs, red first where today fails: seon.ratom-test/a-commit-costs-its-datoms-not-the-readers (T = 1, 100, 10,000; d = 1, 10; :constant in T, <= 2 x 10k ticks a datom; a forced hash collision reruns the other reader, never skips the right one); seon.ratom-test/a-commit-costs-its-datoms-not-the-store (N 10^3 vs 10^5 within 2x); seon.ratom-test/a-diamonds-top-runs-once-a-commit; seon.ratom-test/a-reaction-that-gains-a-deeper-source-runs-once-with-its-final-value; seon.ratom-test/a-deep-chain-raises-its-heights-in-its-length (h = 100, <= 60k ticks); seon.ratom-test/a-cycle-made-by-a-run-is-that-runs-typed-error. See docs/reactive.md. The diff's cost (deps, Datahike B2, 2026-11-15 06:45 [M, root's main in memory]): datahike.db/datoms-diff of plain heads costs 87, 9 and 19 KB a datom for 1, 10 and 100 scattered datoms, 1.1 KB a datom for 100 clustered, and ~60 KB a datom at a merge's d = 7,163 (the whole index decoded on both sides). The alternative, a Datahike read of the commits' datoms in (from, to], was closed with runtime-2 (06:50): advance! keeps the diff of plain heads and no range read is added to Datahike."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.ratom-test/a-commit-costs-its-datoms-not-the-readers seon.ratom-test/a-commit-costs-its-datoms-not-the-store seon.ratom-test/a-diamonds-top-runs-once-a-commit seon.ratom-test/a-reaction-that-gains-a-deeper-source-runs-once-with-its-final-value seon.ratom-test/a-deep-chain-raises-its-heights-in-its-length seon.ratom-test/a-cycle-made-by-a-run-is-that-runs-typed-error}}
 {:seon.task/name "an-owner-step-advances-its-store-and-flushes"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner: runtime; flow reviews (its bars: height order once, atomic effects with a between-reactions budget, cross-owner as port messages). What exists [M]: no production code feeds a store from real commits (the core map, notes runtime-core-map/0-who-benefits-from-the-reactive-core.md); the render proc, the reconciler, the fork server and each agent each diff main and filter by hand lists. Design: one step helper an owner proc calls: binds seon.ratom/*owner* and *tracks* once from its state (E2); takes its port's messages (a dirty from another owner, a resume); on the writer's commit notice advance!s its store (E6; an agent also from its own transact!); flushes by height with auto-run held; a reaction that throws keeps the throw as its value and the flush continues; a work budget, :seon.config.ratom/flush-ticks by owner kind (render, reconciler, agent, fork-server), worked from each owner's lower bound (one commit's typical re-runs x measured cost, x10), checked only between reactions (each effect atomic); spent, the rest stay queued in height order and the owner puts one idempotent {:seon.ratom/resume} on its own port channel (no flag: a throw cannot revert one; a resume on an empty queue is a no-op). Effectful reactions (loading code, the schema registry, config, contract re-arming) run in that step in root, the fork server and each agent. Estimate: overhead O(m + r), ~1k ticks plus ~300 a reaction run. Deletes (as each owner moves, per the map): writer main-commit's hand calls (load-changes!, hold-registry!, cfg/moved), the attr lists moves-program?, schema-moved, config-moved!. Proofs, red first: seon.ratom-test/a-flush-past-its-budget-resumes-on-its-next-step (with a step that throws after its resume is put); seon.ratom-test/a-reaction-runs-only-in-its-owners-step (flow's, kept green). See docs/reactive.md."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.ratom/a-commit-reaches-only-the-readers-of-what-it-moved"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.ratom-test/a-flush-past-its-budget-resumes-on-its-next-step seon.ratom-test/a-reaction-runs-only-in-its-owners-step}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-read-key-is-one-fixnum"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner: runtime (root 21:58, 22:02). What exists [M]: a read key is a boxed Clojure vector [:ea e a] in a hash set, ~135 B a key (trial T9); a health class holds 1,522 (web T2). Measured on main [M]: 1,006 schema keys, the largest eid 1,152,920,505,196,681,680 (60 bits: Datahike's partitions use the high bits), so no split of kind + attribute + e fits a 61-bit fixnum. Rule: a key is one fixnum, a 60-bit hash of [kind a e-or-v], always, no partial packing, and STABLE across processes, versions and Jolt pins, since stored key sets are reused across them (root 22:06): e as a long through splitmix64 (pure arithmetic); a and v by our own FNV-1a-64 over canonical bytes, never Clojure's hash (not promised stable): a keyword's namespace and name as UTF-8, a v through the one codec (seon.edn/encode) to its UTF-8 bytes; a stored key set carries its format, :seon.reads/key-format 1, and a set of another format is read as no reuse; a collision only over-invalidates (the index finds the moved key's readers plus the colliding key's; it never misses); P(any collision) at 10^6 live keys ~ n^2/2^61 ~ 4e-7. A reader's key set is a sorted fxvector (8 B a key; gained/lost by a linear merge); the {key #{reader}} index is keyed by fixnum. Packed at capture and in advance! (deps may emit them from datahike.reads; else ~50 ticks a key in the core [H]). Estimate: 202 + 8k B a reader own, <= 100 B a distinct index key; 10k tracks at k = 10: ~3 MB own + ~8 MB index (boxed ~22 MB). Proofs: seon.ratom-test/a-read-key-is-equal-in-two-processes (GOLDEN values: literal fixnums in the test for a key of each kind, with a keyword, a string, a uuid and a map v, computed once when written; the core must compute exactly those, which holds across processes, restarts and Jolt pins; plus one fresh bin/jolt -e process over the same keys; a fork is no check, since it shares the hash seed (root); red under Clojure's hash); seon.ratom-test/a-track-costs-its-key-set-in-memory (k = 1, 10, 100: <= 2 x (202 + 8k) B own, <= 100 B a distinct index key, live heap after seon.lib/non-static-live!)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.ratom-test/a-read-key-is-equal-in-two-processes seon.ratom-test/a-track-costs-its-key-set-in-memory}}]
